@team
title: Your team
is-pinned-card: true
tags: sp_advisor
view-if: sanchez_leader = 1
new-page: true

= Your team

You can keep up to three advisers at a time (now [+ adv_count +]). Bringing someone in pleases their faction a little; letting them go angers it more. Each faction brings its own kind of help: Institutionalists keep the party together and speak to everyone; Modernisers bring good governance and moderate, liberal voters; the Socialist Left fires up the base and keeps Podemos close; Sanchistas build personal loyalty and protect your position; Trade Unionists win workers and donations; Regional Barons campaign in their regions, calm the other barons and attract moderates. José Luis Ábalos and the government's ministers do not count.

- @hire_hernando: Bring in Antonio Hernando (Institutionalists)
- @hire_luena: Bring in César Luena (Sanchistas)
- @hire_lastra: Bring in Adriana Lastra (Socialist Left)
- @hire_redondo: Bring in Iván Redondo (Modernisers)
- @hire_calvo: Bring in Carmen Calvo (Institutionalists)
- @hire_cerdan: Bring in Santos Cerdán (Sanchistas)
- @hire_tapias: Bring in José Antonio Pérez Tapias (Socialist Left)
- @hire_ferrer: Bring in Toni Ferrer (Trade Unionists)
- @hire_puig: Bring in Ximo Puig (Regional Barons)
- @hire_vara: Bring in Guillermo Fernández Vara (Regional Barons)
- @fire_hernando: Let Antonio Hernando go
- @fire_luena: Let César Luena go
- @fire_lastra: Let Adriana Lastra go
- @fire_redondo: Let Iván Redondo go
- @fire_calvo: Let Carmen Calvo go
- @fire_cerdan: Let Santos Cerdán go
- @fire_tapias: Let José Antonio Pérez Tapias go
- @fire_ferrer: Let Toni Ferrer go
- @fire_puig: Let Ximo Puig go
- @fire_vara: Let Guillermo Fernández Vara go
- @root: Back

